WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }
::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:03.370
Get running, get running

3
00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:06.460
holding our flag high in the sky

4
00:00:12.770 --> 00:00:18.060
Cross this endless sea with me and search for

5
00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:21.810
a global miracle no one

6
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:23.940
has yet been able to find

7
00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:27.960
With our hearts pounding,

8
00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:29.710
we'll just charge ahead as we please, following

9
00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:35.590
the footprints of those who pursue their dreams

10
00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:39.390
No matter how stormy the night,

11
00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:42.390
if we put our minds together,

12
00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:46.540
we'll get through it

13
00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:47.860
always

14
00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:51.590
Get running, get running

15
00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:54.550
holding our flag high in the sky

16
00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:57.140
Even though there are tears

17
00:00:57.230 --> 00:01:00.580
we don't want anyone to see

18
00:01:00.770 --> 00:01:03.520
Keep chasing, keep chasing

19
00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:06.520
the compass that leads to our dreams

20
00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:09.230
always points straight ahead

21
00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:11.400
We can't stop here

22
00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:21.490
Get running, get running,

23
00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:24.540
head past everyone else

24
00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:27.120
So long as we don't run from it,

25
00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:30.540
we can take hold of tomorrow

26
00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:33.630
Keep chasing, keep chasing

27
00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:36.510
everything we see in the moment,

28
00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:38.930
we should record it all

29
00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:41.430
in the blank slates of our minds

30
00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:58.720
<b>Rob Lucci</b>

31
00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:13.320
Th-They're here! The bombardment has started!

32
00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:17.950
Watch out!

33
00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:19.110
Run!

34
00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:20.780
Get us out of here!

35
00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:22.620
I know!

36
00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:29.500
The buster call has begun!

37
00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:34.380
Our targets are Straw Hat Luffy 
and his crew of about sixty pirates!

38
00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:37.380
However, due to a private 
agreement with Admiral Aokiji,

39
00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:42.490
the criminal Nico Robin—last seen on
the Bridge of Hesitation—is not a target.

40
00:02:42.490 --> 00:02:44.280
There's no need to assess the current situation!

41
00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:48.140
Completely destroy the Judicial Island, Enies Lobby!

42
00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:50.140
All battleships, take your positions!

43
00:02:56.650 --> 00:03:02.030
I repeat. Our targets are Straw Hat Luffy
and his crew of about sixty pirates!

44
00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:05.240
Completely destroy Enies Lobby!

45
00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:09.710
Ah... H-Hey!

46
00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:12.900
Hey, look, you guys! Don't run!

47
00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:15.340
See? The battleships aren't attacking the bridge!

48
00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:27.470
That's because I'm here!

49
00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:29.930
That's right. My old man said the same thing.

50
00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:33.310
He was the only one to avoid
the indiscriminate cannon fire!

51
00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:40.030
However, the bridge with the criminal Nico Robin is not a target for now.

52
00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:43.030
Hey! Look at this! This bridge is safe!

53
00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:46.410
It's because I'm the chief of CP9!

54
00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:55.790
What a crazy sight.

55
00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:59.260
Hm? Hey, what's wrong?

56
00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:09.720
I can't stop trembling.

57
00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:36.420
Let's hurry, you guys! Be quick!

58
00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:38.920
Stop bossing us around, you jerk!

59
00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:41.960
If I may say one more thing,
this is aggravating my wounds.

60
00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:45.430
Could you carry me a little more gently?

61
00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:49.720
Don't ask too much! 
Besides, you're contradicting yourself.

62
00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:52.710
It's no exaggeration to say...

63
00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:56.150
that I paid for the glory
of my actions with my entire body!

64
00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:59.070
Ahh! All my ribs are broken! All six of them!

65
00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:01.070
There are more than that, so don't worry.

66
00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:02.820
Seriously, you're such a pain!

67
00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:07.070
By the way, would you like to know
the secret of my new weapon, Kabuto?

68
00:05:07.070 --> 00:05:11.330
I shall explain it to you. Kabuto, Sogeking's weapon, is-

69
00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:13.960
– Ta-da!
– Shut up, you jerk! Or we'll make you run!

70
00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:18.920
Please! Spare me! My ribs
are broken! A-All ten of them.

71
00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:20.750
– There are more than that.
– What?

72
00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:23.760
Then 20... 30?

73
00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:25.090
How about 100?!

74
00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:26.220
There are more than that!

75
00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:28.590
No way that's true!

76
00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:35.310
What's that?

77
00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:42.280
Water!

78
00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:45.320
What the heck is going on?!

79
00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:52.290
Why is there water?! What?!
Why?! We have no way out!

80
00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:53.950
Help!

81
00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:14.350
I don't care whether anyone's in the corridor or not.

82
00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:16.230
No one can get here now.

83
00:06:16.230 --> 00:06:17.810
You bastard!

84
00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:21.360
Soon this room will be underwater.

85
00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:30.870
You bastard!

86
00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:54.060
This room is above sea level.
The water won't reach here.

87
00:06:55.640 --> 00:06:59.390
You can hear the sounds of the
battleships' cannon fire, right?

88
00:07:05.730 --> 00:07:11.740
What happened to your crew?
What happened to Nico Robin?

89
00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:14.450
You must be worried.

90
00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:26.710
If you wanna go rescue them, go right ahead.

91
00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:30.510
I won't let you out of my sight.

92
00:07:35.050 --> 00:07:39.390
No matter what they're going through
right now, they'll survive for sure!

93
00:07:39.390 --> 00:07:44.060
But if I let you get away now,
you'll go kill my friends!

94
00:07:44.060 --> 00:07:47.530
I won't let you out of my sight!

95
00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:06.380
The bombardment has begun.

96
00:08:06.380 --> 00:08:10.210
By the way, I can hear a strange sound up ahead.

97
00:08:10.210 --> 00:08:11.420
Shut your mouth!

98
00:08:11.420 --> 00:08:13.220
Nooo!

99
00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:15.510
Grandma! What's going on?!

100
00:08:15.510 --> 00:08:18.760
Who cares?! Hurry up and run!

101
00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:24.190
You make a pretty good boss.

102
00:08:24.190 --> 00:08:27.020
I wish an idiot I know could hear you.

103
00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:31.280
But I wonder, do you have the ability to back up your decision?

104
00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:38.240
The result will be the same if you die!

105
00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:04.810
Hey! Capture Nico Robin already!

106
00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:09.150
Once this is all over, I'll be the world's hero!

107
00:09:09.150 --> 00:09:13.280
The buster call sounds like a gun salute for me!

108
00:09:27.100 --> 00:09:27.920
Razor!

109
00:09:30.340 --> 00:09:31.710
Finger Pistol!

110
00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:35.240
Tempest Kick: Leopard Tail!

111
00:09:42.890 --> 00:09:44.810
Can you really defeat me?!

112
00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:48.560
I can't protect anyone unless I win!

113
00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:54.780
Rubber Rubber...

114
00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:58.820
Rifle!

115
00:09:58.820 --> 00:10:01.040
Iron Body: Fruitless Shrub.

116
00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:16.670
Razor!

117
00:10:19.890 --> 00:10:24.220
I salute you for having the guts to pick
a fight with the World Government.

118
00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:46.870
Rubber Rubber Pistol!

119
00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:53.540
Flying Finger Pistol:

120
00:10:57.760 --> 00:10:58.800
Sting!

121
00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:12.690
Triple Sting!

122
00:11:31.750 --> 00:11:33.500
Flying Finger Pistol:

123
00:11:34.290 --> 00:11:35.380
Fire Sting!

124
00:11:49.180 --> 00:11:54.610
I thought I'd met a man with some backbone. How disappointing.

125
00:11:54.610 --> 00:11:58.980
So you did run out of strength from your doping earlier?

126
00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:09.500
If it's backbone you want, I'll show you...

127
00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:11.960
another tactic!

128
00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:14.540
Gear Third!

129
00:12:24.430 --> 00:12:25.970
Bone Balloon!

130
00:12:27.050 --> 00:12:28.430
Bone?

131
00:12:28.430 --> 00:12:31.060
The power moves from one bone to another.

132
00:12:32.430 --> 00:12:34.690
Take a look! My left arm is...

133
00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:39.320
the arm of a giant!

134
00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:42.280
If it's all show, don't even bother!

135
00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:44.780
Rubber Rubber...

136
00:12:44.780 --> 00:12:45.740
Iron Body!

137
00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:48.740
Gigant Pistol!

138
00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:02.630
Wh-What the hell is that?!

139
00:13:20.690 --> 00:13:25.450
I feel like I'm about to pass out.
I can't fall into the sea like this!

140
00:13:40.960 --> 00:13:42.170
Oops!

141
00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:51.310
What was that?

142
00:13:51.310 --> 00:13:53.270
Hurry and help the injured!

143
00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:00.230
Who are you?!

144
00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:02.650
– A beast?!
– No, he has an ability!

145
00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:09.070
I landed on the deck of a battleship.
That was close.

146
00:14:09.070 --> 00:14:10.740
He flew from the bridge.

147
00:14:10.740 --> 00:14:11.780
Is he a pirate?

148
00:14:11.780 --> 00:14:14.580
I saw a huge hand, too!

149
00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:17.290
Stop! Stop! I said stop!

150
00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:21.340
It's dangerous up ahead!
Water is rushing towards us!

151
00:14:21.340 --> 00:14:23.930
C-Can't you guys hear the sound of water?!

152
00:14:23.930 --> 00:14:26.760
Listen, if the water flows into
an underground passage like this,

153
00:14:26.760 --> 00:14:28.970
we'll have no choice but to drown.

154
00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:31.800
Zoro-kun, can't you hear the sound of water?!

155
00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:35.430
Hmm, I agree that something doesn't feel right.

156
00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:37.390
Then let's stop already!

157
00:14:37.390 --> 00:14:40.100
There's no other way. We have to keep going!

158
00:14:43.770 --> 00:14:45.090
I knew it!

159
00:14:45.090 --> 00:14:47.280
Water is about to overwhelm Nami and the others!

160
00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:51.570
Ah! Pirate guys!

161
00:14:52.030 --> 00:14:54.740
Guys! Do something about this water!

162
00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:56.660
Do something?! What're we supposed to do?!

163
00:14:56.660 --> 00:14:59.920
See, I told you! This passage is
gonna be flooded with water!

164
00:14:59.920 --> 00:15:01.130
N-Nami-san...

165
00:15:01.130 --> 00:15:03.240
is rushing into my arms!

166
00:15:03.240 --> 00:15:04.140
How optimistic!

167
00:15:04.140 --> 00:15:06.170
This is bad! We're gonna be trapped in here!

168
00:15:09.970 --> 00:15:12.470
I can't cut it! It's not iron or stone?!

169
00:15:12.470 --> 00:15:14.140
This is an undersea passage.

170
00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:17.470
It must be made of some damn thick steel
that can bear the water pressure!

171
00:15:17.470 --> 00:15:19.770
Then there's nowhere to run!

172
00:15:20.350 --> 00:15:21.980
Ahh! It's here!

173
00:15:30.610 --> 00:15:32.780
It isn't safe here! We're gonna die!

174
00:15:32.780 --> 00:15:34.200
Hurry!

175
00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:37.240
We're doomed! The sea train won't start!

176
00:15:37.240 --> 00:15:39.160
Where's the engineer?!

177
00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:42.420
Let's get outta here! Come on!

178
00:15:50.510 --> 00:15:51.720
Vice Admiral!

179
00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:54.680
What do we do about capturing 
Nico Robin on the Bridge of Hesitation?!

180
00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:56.970
– Leave her alone.
– But...

181
00:15:56.970 --> 00:15:59.480
As long as that man is on this island,

182
00:15:59.480 --> 00:16:01.940
with the mission of escorting Nico Robin,

183
00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:04.900
we don't have to get involved.

184
00:16:05.730 --> 00:16:09.360
We'll just burn down everything but the Bridge of Hesitation.

185
00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:10.440
Yes, sir!

186
00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:12.070
Vice Admiral,

187
00:16:12.070 --> 00:16:16.490
is the man you mentioned Rob Lucci of CP9?

188
00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:24.540
As we suspected, he has a devil fruit ability!

189
00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:28.340
Who the hell are you?!

190
00:16:30.880 --> 00:16:33.300
We're asking who you are! Answer us!

191
00:16:33.300 --> 00:16:35.550
Stand down, you idiots!

192
00:16:35.550 --> 00:16:36.470
Captain?!

193
00:16:36.970 --> 00:16:38.810
Put down your guns!

194
00:16:38.810 --> 00:16:41.180
Who do you think you're talking to?!

195
00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:44.980
He is Rob Lucci of CP9!

196
00:16:52.360 --> 00:16:53.860
R-Rob Lucci-san!

197
00:16:53.860 --> 00:16:55.450
What?! That's...

198
00:16:55.450 --> 00:16:57.530
We're sorry! Please spare us!

199
00:16:57.530 --> 00:17:00.240
Keep your mouths shut. Your whining is grating.

200
00:17:06.580 --> 00:17:09.880
I've heard a lot about Rob Lucci,

201
00:17:09.880 --> 00:17:11.550
but is he really that good?

202
00:17:12.800 --> 00:17:15.880
It was fifteen years ago...

203
00:17:15.880 --> 00:17:17.970
In one kingdom,

204
00:17:17.970 --> 00:17:21.720
pirates captured some 500 soldiers.

205
00:17:24.060 --> 00:17:29.440
In exchange for the hostages' lives,
the pirate captain demanded the throne.

206
00:17:29.440 --> 00:17:32.610
The World Government sent a boy to the kingdom,

207
00:17:32.610 --> 00:17:37.570
as it was on the verge of surrender,
due to its concern for the hostages.

208
00:17:39.030 --> 00:17:40.160
A-A child?

209
00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:43.830
Dammit! That blasted World
Government! How insulting!

210
00:17:48.250 --> 00:17:49.220
Shave!

211
00:17:55.090 --> 00:17:56.090
Tempest Kick!

212
00:18:14.360 --> 00:18:17.610
He infiltrated the pirates' hideout...

213
00:18:17.610 --> 00:18:22.530
and killed all 500 of the kingdom's soldiers on the spot.

214
00:18:22.530 --> 00:18:24.750
He k-killed all of them?

215
00:18:24.750 --> 00:18:28.000
That can't be! How could he be forgiven for that?!

216
00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:31.960
Even if it's the World Government...
Even if it's for justice...

217
00:18:33.380 --> 00:18:35.210
P-Pardon me!

218
00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:39.930
<b>Justice</b>

219
00:18:35.960 --> 00:18:39.930
Listen up. Justice isn't all warm and fuzzy!

220
00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:42.220
None of you forget it!

221
00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:43.350
Yes, sir!

222
00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:47.020
The pirates were so enraged that they rained fire upon the boy,

223
00:18:47.020 --> 00:18:50.810
who was standing on the pile of bodies with his back turned.

224
00:18:51.810 --> 00:18:57.280
But the boy rose from the flames, killed the pirate captain,

225
00:18:57.690 --> 00:19:00.700
and single-handedly put the whole affair to rest.

226
00:19:02.910 --> 00:19:05.790
Wh-What the hell is this?!

227
00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:12.460
How dare you kill our valuable hostages?!

228
00:19:12.460 --> 00:19:14.420
They committed a crime,

229
00:19:15.170 --> 00:19:17.920
so I executed them in the name of justice.

230
00:19:17.920 --> 00:19:19.300
A crime?

231
00:19:19.300 --> 00:19:22.970
As soldiers of the kingdom, being weak is a crime.

232
00:19:22.970 --> 00:19:24.810
Guys! Take him down!

233
00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:43.070
H-How could he have survived that?!

234
00:19:47.460 --> 00:19:48.580
Shave!

235
00:19:56.110 --> 00:19:57.000
Finger Pistol.

236
00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:07.100
Captain!

237
00:20:07.100 --> 00:20:09.060
H-He's a monster!

238
00:20:09.060 --> 00:20:10.350
Help!

239
00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:17.520
The boy with several cannonball scars on his back...

240
00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:21.190
was a CP9 intelligence agent at the age of 13.

241
00:20:21.190 --> 00:20:24.610
Some call him the most powerful and ruthless mass killing machine...

242
00:20:24.610 --> 00:20:28.740
in the history of CP9 and its mission of covert justice.

243
00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:32.160
It's unreal that he was capable of
all that when he was only 13.

244
00:20:32.160 --> 00:20:37.210
That's precisely why all we have to do is carry out our duty.

245
00:20:38.040 --> 00:20:39.920
Rubber Rubber...

246
00:20:39.920 --> 00:20:42.550
Rocket!

247
00:20:42.550 --> 00:20:43.930
What is it this time?!

248
00:20:44.430 --> 00:20:46.300
Something came out!

249
00:20:46.300 --> 00:20:49.260
That's Straw Hat Luffy, 
whose bounty is 100 million belly!

250
00:20:49.260 --> 00:20:50.560
I didn't think he'd be that fat.

251
00:20:50.560 --> 00:20:52.680
There you are! Pigeon guy!

252
00:20:52.680 --> 00:20:54.190
Shoot him down!

253
00:20:57.440 --> 00:21:00.320
That won't work! The Bone Balloon is tough!

254
00:21:05.410 --> 00:21:09.790
Rubber Rubber Gigant Axe!

255
00:21:12.120 --> 00:21:13.290
Ahhh!

256
00:21:13.290 --> 00:21:15.420
What the hell?! Is it a giant?!

257
00:21:45.700 --> 00:21:49.450
Rubber Rubber Gigant Whip!

258
00:21:52.240 --> 00:21:54.330
Whoa! Watch out!

259
00:21:54.330 --> 00:21:55.710
The masts snapped!

260
00:21:55.710 --> 00:21:57.790
They're collapsing!

261
00:21:57.790 --> 00:22:01.210
The fight between those two is insane!

262
00:22:03.170 --> 00:22:05.260
Finger Pistol: Sting!

263
00:22:08.680 --> 00:22:12.010
It seems that as you grow more powerful, you become slower.

264
00:22:16.640 --> 00:22:18.650
Tempest Kick: Victory Bird!

265
00:22:28.410 --> 00:22:30.910
He cracked the iron hull!

266
00:22:30.910 --> 00:22:32.450
This ship won't last long!

267
00:22:37.120 --> 00:22:39.670
That was close. I almost got split in two.

268
00:22:45.550 --> 00:22:47.300
Did you see that, Cutty Flam?!

269
00:22:47.300 --> 00:22:51.800
It's all over for you guys! 
Or rather, it was all over from the start!

270
00:22:51.800 --> 00:22:54.430
It's a bit early to say that
when the fight isn't over yet!

271
00:22:54.430 --> 00:22:57.100
Lucci is the one fighting Straw Hat.

272
00:22:57.100 --> 00:22:59.310
He's the strongest man in the history of CP9!

273
00:22:59.310 --> 00:23:01.980
You might've managed to get rid of the others somehow,

274
00:23:01.980 --> 00:23:04.270
but Lucci's another story entirely!

275
00:23:04.270 --> 00:23:09.110
Once Straw Hat's taken care of,
you're next, Cutty Flam!

276
00:23:09.780 --> 00:23:11.870
I'm counting on you, Straw Hat!

277
00:23:11.870 --> 00:23:15.290
What's going on? Give me a report.

278
00:23:15.290 --> 00:23:17.370
Yes, sir, Vice Admiral!

279
00:23:17.370 --> 00:23:21.790
We heard that Straw Hat Luffy and
Rob Lucci of CP9 are currently fighting.

280
00:23:21.790 --> 00:23:23.920
As a result, battleship No. 4 is in bad shape!

281
00:23:23.920 --> 00:23:27.130
Rob Lucci isn't gonna die.

282
00:23:27.130 --> 00:23:31.680
All gunners, target battleship No. 4!

283
00:23:31.680 --> 00:23:33.800
Prepare all guns for a volley in five seconds!

284
00:23:34.220 --> 00:23:36.060
What?! Vice Admiral, you must be kidding.

285
00:23:36.060 --> 00:23:38.100
One thousand of our men are onboard!

286
00:23:49.530 --> 00:23:53.070
A moment's indecision can allow
vicious criminals to slip away.

287
00:23:53.070 --> 00:23:56.030
Can you protect our future from them?

288
00:24:06.840 --> 00:24:08.050
Fire!
